packages.description:
ADR 0005 §3.2.

`openSqliteDb(path, {log})` returns `Db & {exec, close, raw}` over node:sqlite `Database`:
- startup pragmas, read back and asserted;
- nested `tx`: BEGIN IMMEDIATE outside, SAVEPOINT/RELEASE/ROLLBACK TO inside; Promise-returning callbacks refused;
- the existing `checkParams`; ArrayBuffer conversion of BLOB reads; `rowsWritten = changes`;
- a multi-statement tokenizer;
- an authorizer denying TRANSACTION, SAVEPOINT, PRAGMA, ATTACH and DETACH for module SQL;
- `SqlRangeError` for integers above 2^53;
- a 256-entry statement LRU;
- `locking_mode=EXCLUSIVE` before the first WAL access: the single-writer lock that makes a second process or connection on the same file fail (ADR §3.2, §3.10);
- `busyTimeoutMs` is an option (production 5000, read back through `PRAGMA busy_timeout`); tests pass 200 so nothing waits 5 s;
- `{create: false}` (the default for main.ts) refuses a missing file instead of creating an empty database.

migrate.ts accepts a `MigrationTarget {exec, tx}` and keeps its current DO-storage overload for index-do.ts until N7-01. It applies the §3.2 compatibility rule: a database newer than the code is ready when `schema_compat.min_compatible_version` (absent table: the database version) is at most the code version, else too_new. The test builds synthetic migration lists, so it does not depend on N1-10.

test/node/support/node-db.ts exports `withMigratedDb(fn)` over a temporary file and `reopen(db)`. Every later worker-node test uses it.

ADR 0005 §3.3.

`NodeAlarm implements AlarmStorage` over one setTimeout:
- delays clamped to 2^31−1 ms, re-armed until the wall-clock due time;
- callback errors caught and logged, then re-armed at now + backoff;
- `startHeartbeat(core, 30 s)` fires overdue timers after a suspend;
- `startEnsureRunning(core, 5 min)` replaces cron.

All timers are injectable (fake timers plus fixedClock) and unref'd. `stop()` clears everything for shutdown.

ADR 0005 §3.4.

**Connector** (`connectJetstreamWs(url, opts)` with the `ws` package):
- https→wss mapping;
- `unexpected-response` → `JetstreamConnectError {status, xrpcError, cursorRejected}`;
- maxPayload 1 MiB, perMessageDeflate off, 10 s handshake timeout;
- Buffer→ArrayBuffer LinkEvents, buffered until start();
- close(1000);
- only hosts in JETSTREAM_URLS.

**fake-jetstream.ts** gains `memoryLink()`, an in-memory JetstreamLink connector that works on any host, and keeps its WebSocketPair export for workerd users until N7-01.

**packages/atproto** switches to `environment: 'node'`; its 47 tests pass unchanged.

**Runtime-neutral scaffold check (ADR §15.3).** packages/atproto/test/scaffold.test.ts:9 asserts `navigator.userAgent === 'Cloudflare-Workers'`. Replace that assertion, keeping the title, with runtime-neutral checks: WebCrypto ECDSA P-256 sign and verify round-trip, and NFKC normalisation present. The connector passes `rejectUnauthorized: true` to ws explicitly (ADR §3.4).

ADR 0005 §3.6, §3.7.

**http-bridge.ts** (`createServer({publicOrigin, listen, handler, caps})`):
- WHATWG Request/Response bridge with the URL built from PUBLIC_ORIGIN;
- Host check (421);
- per-route streamed body caps (413 after cap+1 bytes); AbortSignal on client disconnect; HEAD;
- keepAliveTimeout 100 s, headersTimeout 60 s, requestTimeout 600 s;
- loopback-only `ATMUSIC_LISTEN` parsing;
- LISTEN_FDS socket activation with the loopback check.

**static-assets.ts:**
- in-memory web/dist; the `_headers` parser;
- ETag/304; MIME table; /index.html → 301 /;
- 405 JSON envelope for non-GET to an existing file;
- traversal refusal; `_headers` never served.

**client-ip.ts:** the trusted-peer CIDR rule, cf-connecting-ip, rightmost-untrusted x-forwarded-for, x-real-ip, none. The mode has no default (N1-07 makes it required), and only the header named by the mode is ever read. Ported from crates/server/src/http/limits.rs:138-191.

**Rate keys and bucket sets (ADR §3.6, §8.7, §13).** client-ip.ts exports `rateKeyOf(ip)`: the IPv4 address, or the /64 prefix of an IPv6 address. limits.ts `BucketSet` gains an `onFull: 'refuse' | 'evict-lru'` option. `refuse` (the default) keeps today's behaviour, so worker/test/http/limits.test.ts (worker-modules, ported by N2-02) is unchanged; `evict-lru` drops the least recently used bucket when MAX_BUCKET_KEYS (10,000) keys are live and admits the new key. Every per-IP set built for the Node host uses `evict-lru` and `rateKeyOf`; per-credential sets use `refuse`.

ADR 0005 §3.8.

**config.ts:** `parseNodeConfig(env)` returns `NodeConfig`, which embeds `parseConfig` from worker/src/config.ts. It adds every §3.8 variable, the https rules, INGEST_MODE socket|off, and the refusal of pulse. **Workers-era variables (ADR §3.8):** parseConfig still requires PLAN and DO_LOCATION_HINT and builds its budget from BUDGETS[plan]; parseNodeConfig passes `PLAN='paid'` and `DO_LOCATION_HINT=''` to it internally and rejects any operator-set PLAN or DO_LOCATION_HINT with a ConfigError citing ADR 0005. N7-01 removes them from config.ts.

**Runtime environment (ADR §3.8, §14.1):** `FORBIDDEN_RUNTIME_ENV` lists NODE_OPTIONS, NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED, NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS, NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY, NODE_PATH, HTTP_PROXY, http_proxy, HTTPS_PROXY, https_proxy, NO_PROXY, no_proxy, ALL_PROXY, all_proxy, SSL_CERT_FILE and SSL_CERT_DIR; `checkRuntimeEnv(env)` returns a ConfigError naming the first one present (run() exits 78 on it, N3-07; the unit unsets them, N4-02).

**Process timings:** NodeConfig carries `busyTimeoutMs` 5000 and `drainMs` 25000 as fixed production values (not environment variables); tests construct smaller values directly. ATMUSIC_CLIENT_IP_HEADER is required (no default; ADR §3.6). ATMUSIC_SIGNIN_POLICY (allowlist default) with ATMUSIC_SIGNIN_DIDS, ATMUSIC_UPLOAD_MAX_BYTES and ATMUSIC_MIN_FREE_BYTES are parsed here. No environment variable relaxes a rule: only the test-only option `{fixtureOrigins: true}`, which the e2e entry passes and main.ts never does, allows http origins and fixture upstreams.

**secrets.ts** reads `$CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/secrets`, or `ATMUSIC_SECRETS_FILE` only when its mode is 0600 or stricter, and validates:
- cursorKey of at least 32 bytes;
- encryptionKeys with unique ids and 32-byte keys;
- oauthSigningKeys as private ES256 JWKs with unique kids;
- oauthAnnouncedKeys holding public keys only;
- the optional lastfm block.

Secrets are never copied into process.env, and ConfigError messages never contain values.

**gen-secrets.ts** writes fresh keys to stdout or a 0600 file with local randomness, and supports `--oauth-key <kid>`.

**disk.ts:** `freeBytes(path)` over `fs.statfs` and `diskLow(path, minFree)`; injectable for tests. Used by readiness (N2-01), the OAuth keepalive and store (N2-03), backups (N3-07) and the import writer (N3-09).

ADR 0005 §5.10, §15.2. All fakes are deterministic, clock-driven and reachable only through router-transport hostnames (as.test and pds*.test); routerTransport already accepts arbitrary endpoints through its `hosts` option, so router-transport.ts is not changed. The Last.fm and ListenBrainz fakes need MD5 and Node types, so they live under worker/test/node/support/ (N1-13).

**fake-oauth-as:**
- PAR, auto-approving authorize, token;
- private_key_jwt verification against the client's jwks_uri, fetched through the router transport;
- the 60 s assertion age and jti uniqueness rules;
- DPoP nonce rotation, refresh, invalid_grant, revoke (every revocation recorded);
- client-metadata re-fetch with a 10 min cache.

**fake-pds** additions, with existing behaviour unchanged:
- applyWrites: atomic, ≤ 200 writes, ≤ 1,000,000 bytes;
- **DPoP is opt-in per account** (ADR §5.10): `addAccount(repo, {handle, auth: 'dpop'})` makes createRecord, deleteRecord and applyWrites for that account require a DPoP-bound access token from fake-oauth-as; the default `auth: 'fixture'` keeps accepting `fixtureToken(did)` Bearer tokens, so packages/atproto/test/fixture-kit.test.ts (:595-606, :853) and test-support/read-models.ts:171 keep working unchanged;
- RateLimit-* headers from a points ledger (create 3, update 2, delete 1); 429 when exhausted.

ADR 0005 §15.2. Last.fm's api_sig is MD5, WebCrypto has no MD5, and packages/atproto/test-support compiles without Node types (lib es2024 + dom), so these fakes live in worker/test/node/support/ and use node:crypto createHash('md5') directly. They do not import worker/src/crypto/md5.ts (N1-08, same wave); the test pins the same vector N1-08 pins. Each fake is a routerTransport endpoint (the existing `hosts` option), mounted at lastfm.test and listenbrainz.test by later suites, and is also startable as a loopback HTTP server for the e2e stacks (N6-01, N8-01).

**fake-lastfm:**
- verifies api_sig with its configured secret on signed methods;
- auth.getSession; track.scrobble (≤ 50, records the inputs); updateNowPlaying; love and unlove;
- paged user.getRecentTracks over a seeded history with a fixed `to`, with a nowplaying row on page 1;
- scripted error codes and HTTP statuses, including a per-item ignoredMessage code 5.

**fake-listenbrainz:** validate-token, recording submit-listens, paged listens by max_ts, X-RateLimit-* headers, scripted 401, 429 and 503.

All are deterministic and clock-driven.

ADR 0005 §5.8. This ports web/src/outbox semantics (and crates/server/src/workers/outbox.rs) to the server over the operations, operation_deps, listen_keys and pds_budget tables.

**Kept exactly:**
- the retry formula and exactly 10 attempts;
- persist-before-send with a TID allocated once and a digest;
- ambiguous-create reconciliation and never-overwrite;
- swapRecord deletes;
- predecessors;
- follow and unfollow rules;
- the settings record.

**Added:**
- love.put and love.delete;
- origins and priorities;
- applyWrites batching (≤ 200 writes, ≤ 1,000,000 bytes) with bisection;
- the per-DID point budget honouring RateLimit-* and 429;
- blocked state for reauth_required;
- after each success, the record hint queued with `enqueueHints` (source notify), not the client notify RPC and its abuse buckets; a DID without a users row is admitted instead (ADR §5.8);
- `cancelled` state for a not-yet-sent create (listen key and unsent forward rows deleted), and a chained delete for a running one, used by library.removeScrobble;
- `acceptListens(m, {did, origin, listens, receiptMs})` (ingress.ts): the one shared ingress transaction for /2.0, /1 and web scrobbles. It writes listen keys (idempotent), applies the daily cap, creates operations and calls `enqueueForwards` (forward-enqueue.ts) for the DID's active links with the matching forward flags. enqueueForwards computes dedupe_key per kind (ADR §12.2): the listen key for scrobble, sha256(did‖started_at_ms‖artist_key‖track_key) for nowplaying, and the operation id for love and unlove.

`PdsWriter` abstracts session.fetchHandler, whose requests go through policyFetch (N1-05).

**Deferred listens (ADR §8.3):** acceptListens takes an optional per-listen `notBeforeMs`; when set, the operation's `due_at` and the record's `createdAt` are `notBeforeMs` (listened_at − 300 s), while the listen key and forward rows are written at once. The `outbox` timer and pdsBudget never send an operation before its due_at. The `outbox` extension timer is exported for composition. Test titles from web/test/outbox/* are kept where the behaviour is kept, so that N5-01 can remap the case map.

ADR 0005 §9, §10.

**Modules** `(m: ModuleDeps, args)`:
- `rangeStats({did, entity, lower, upper, limit, offset})` with totals and album-artist grouping, plus the exact cache;
- `recentListens({did, after, before, limit, offset | minTs, maxTs, count})`;
- `lovedTracks`;
- the now-playing store (upsert with TTL, same-track refresh, share_now_playing);
- `activity` (listening and daily);
- `lookupUser(name)` with the §9 order: did: values, dotless usernames, a dotted username only while it equals its owner's current verified handle, then verified handles;
- `recentListens` also takes an artist and track filter for user.getTrackScrobbles.

The existing worker/src/do/read/stats.ts is not touched. Tests seed through the real apply path where the fixture allows, and directly into loves and now_playing otherwise.

ADR 0005 §7.3, §7.7, §7.8.

**Exports:**
- `authMethods` and `writeMethods`, the method tables for /2.0 dispatch (wired in N3-04 routes.ts);
- the /api/auth and /api/auth/ redirect routes (multi-scrobbler omits the slash);
- `POST /api/v1/lastfm/authorize`.

**Behaviour:**
- track.scrobble, track.updateNowPlaying, track.love, track.unlove and library.removeScrobble;
- the shared acceptListens transaction from N2-05 (listen keys, operations, forward rows);
- ignored codes 1–5;
- the daily cap;
- rate limits on getMobileSession keyed by (username, IP) and by IP;
- library.removeScrobble matching indexed records and the caller's unindexed creates at that second, with error 7 for no match (ADR §7.5).

Signatures are verified only for the auth and write methods (requiresSignature, N2-07).

ADR 0005 §7.1, §7.5, §7.9.

**routes.ts** mounts GET and POST on /2.0 and /2.0/ and dispatches by method over the authMethods and writeMethods tables (imported from N3-03 at composition through a registry argument; no import cycle) and the read tables. It enforces api_key, POST-only for writes, CORS on reads, and logs without query strings.

**Read methods:**
- user.getRecentTracks, getTrackScrobbles (Pano GNU FM accounts; the recent-tracks engine with a track filter), getInfo, getTopArtists/Albums/Tracks, getLovedTracks, getWeeklyChartList and the weekly charts, getFriends;
- library.getArtists;
- track/artist/album.getInfo;
- the getTopTags family (empty).

**as12.ts:** the reserved /audioscrobbler/ path. A 1.2 handshake answers the §7.10 FAILED line, also when sent to the root (`GET /?hs=true`, dispatched to the router by N2-01).

**Round 2.** Reads ignore api_sig and use a supplied sk only to identify the caller (ADR §7.3); an unknown sk on a read is ignored, never error 9. Paged lists always serialise as arrays with @attr (N2-07 list flag).

ADR 0005 §8.4–§8.7.

**Endpoints:**
- user/{u}/listens, playing-now, listen-count;
- stats artists/releases/release-groups/recordings, listening-activity, daily-activity;
- feedback recording-feedback and get-feedback;
- following and followers.

**routes.ts** mounts all /1/ routes (including N3-05's, through a registry argument) with CORS, the per-IP and per-token limits, and the 404 envelope.

recording-feedback resolves an MSID through indexed scrobbles, the now_playing row and not-yet-indexed scrobble.create operations, recomputing the MSID of each candidate (ADR §8.6).

Limits use the credential-first limiter of N2-08: an authenticated request is charged to its token only and is never refused because the per-IP set is full.

ADR 0005 §12.

**Linking:**
- the Last.fm web-auth link flow with single-use link_states;
- ListenBrainz token linking through validate-token;
- sealed credentials;
- PATCH and DELETE routes.

**Delivery:**
- the `forward` extension timer;
- signed Last.fm batches of ≤ 50, with the global 1 rps bucket (`upstream-pacing.ts`, shared with imports);
- ListenBrainz single, import ≤ 100 and playing_now;
- feedback by MBID.

**Failure handling:** retry and backoff, 13-day expiry, revocation and hold, the global pause on 10/26 surfaced in adminStatus, and now-playing sent once.

Upstream hosts come from config, and tests use lastfm.test and listenbrainz.test.

Forward rows are created by N2-05 (enqueueForwards, with the per-kind dedupe keys of ADR §12.2); this package delivers them. Last.fm ignored code 5 is re-queued at the next 00:00 UTC; ListenBrainz rows have their own 30-day expiry.

**Round 2.** The Last.fm and ListenBrainz forward clients send through policyFetch (N1-05); fake-lastfm and fake-listenbrainz come from worker/test/node/support (N1-13). DELETE /api/v1/links/{id} journals the deletion (N1-08).

ADR 0005 §14.

**Units and scripts:**
- the units exactly as §14.1, including the three UnsetEnvironment= lines (NODE_OPTIONS, NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED, NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS, NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY, NODE_PATH, both cases of HTTP_PROXY, HTTPS_PROXY, NO_PROXY and ALL_PROXY, SSL_CERT_FILE and SSL_CERT_DIR);
- install-local.sh: build into ~/.local/lib/atmusic/releases/<sha> with `npm ci --ignore-scripts`, run `main.mjs --init` once when the database is missing, atomic current switch, install units, print the linger and enable commands, run them only with --enable;
- restore.ts (§14.5): stop atmusic.socket and atmusic.service and verify both inactive; copy the live db to atmusic.db.pre-restore; migrate the backup copy to the code's schema version; **with a readable live db, replace every non-derived table of TABLE_CLASS (N1-10) wholesale with the live rows and keep only the derived tables from the backup** (an unclassified table aborts); with an unreadable live db refuse unless --accept-loss, which **deletes every web_sessions row and replays revocations.log** (N1-08) into the copy; then open atmusic.db.restore.tmp with journal_mode=DELETE, close it and assert no restore.tmp-wal, -shm or -journal exists; fsync it; delete the live -wal, -shm and -journal and fsync the directory; rename over atmusic.db and fsync the directory again; start both units;
- atmusic-admin.ts (status, backup, resnapshot, prune-kid over the admin socket).

**Docs:** secrets setup, key rotation, upgrades and rollback (link switch only; additive migrations), restore as disaster recovery, Gentoo notes, health, sleep, same-UID exposure and the dedicated-user option. docs/deploy/exposure.md gives per option the required ATMUSIC_CLIENT_IP_HEADER and the proxy directive (ADR §14.6): A, cloudflared with cf-connecting-ip; B, DNS-only Caddy `header_up -CF-Connecting-IP` and `header_up X-Forwarded-For {remote_host}` or nginx `proxy_set_header CF-Connecting-IP ""` and `proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $remote_addr` with x-forwarded-for, stated as valid only without the Cloudflare proxy; C, proxied DNS with mandatory Authenticated Origin Pulls, a firewall admitting only Cloudflare ranges, and Caddy `trusted_proxies static <Cloudflare ranges>` with `client_ip_headers Cf-Connecting-Ip` and `header_up X-Forwarded-For {client_ip}`, or nginx `set_real_ip_from <Cloudflare ranges>` with `real_ip_header CF-Connecting-IP`, with x-forwarded-for; the Cloudflare range list is a dated snapshot with its source URL. All tests use a temporary HOME and never call the real systemctl or loginctl.

ADR 0005 §15.1, §15.3. These projects switch to `environment: 'node'` over compose() (N2-01) and run() (N3-07) with the fixture transport, the memoryLink Jetstream and fixedClock. The test entries (worker/test/acceptance/entry.ts and the composition entries) become Node composition factories that override dependencies through compose options instead of IndexDO.buildDeps.

Titles are kept, except for:
- the index-do and IndexDO-specific RPC tests, which become IndexCore tests;
- scheduled.test.ts, which becomes the ensureRunning-interval test;
- bench row budgets, which become plan assertions with timings reported.

Restart is close-and-reopen of the same file plus a recomposed app. composition/admin.test.ts is ported from the Workers TCP admin route to the admin socket (N3-07); the TCP route itself is deleted by N7-01. These suites stop importing worker/test/write/support.ts and worker/test/fixtures/jetstream-server.ts through cloudflare:* (N4-04 owns those helpers). scripts/benchmark-read-models.ts drops its workerd, wrangler and vitestPlugin environment fields (:110) and records node and sqlite versions instead, so nothing in it refers to Workers when N7-01 runs its no-Workers test.

ADR 0005 §5.9. Remove @atproto/oauth-client-browser and regenerate the lockfile.

**Deleted:**
- web/src/oauth/* — and its importers change here: web/src/main.tsx (imports ./oauth/types and globs ./oauth/session.ts at :10 and :14) boots web/src/session/client.ts instead, and web/src/state/store.ts (:13 imports PdsSession from ../oauth/types) holds the server Session DTO {did, handle, username, csrfToken, status, expiresAt} in place of PdsSession, so tsc -b stays green;
- web/src/outbox/* except overlay.ts;
- routes/callback.tsx.

**Added:**
- the session client (csrfToken; credentials same-origin);
- writes with Idempotency-Key, and operation and record-status polling into the overlay;
- migration.ts, which deletes the legacy atmusic* IndexedDB databases;
- screens /settings/links, /settings/imports (progress, ETA, cancel), /settings/credentials (secret shown once) and /lastfm/authorize.

**Config:** spa-routes drops /oauth/callback and adds the new routes. gen-config imports CLIENT_NAME from packages/core/src/client-name.ts (N2-03), stops emitting oauth/client-metadata.json, sets connect-src 'self', and takes PUBLIC_ORIGIN and LEXICON_PREFIX from --origin/--prefix or config/atmusic.env.example instead of worker/wrangler.jsonc.

**Tests:** web/test/oauth and web/test/outbox are deleted. ts-case-map.json and node-port-inventory.json remap their cases to the N2-03, N2-04, N2-05 and N3-01 tests.

ADR 0005 §15. node-backend.sh replaces the interim node-interim.sh (N0-02) and the retired workers-backend.sh, and mirrors workers-backend.sh: --out with its gate marker, --skip counted as a failure, per-step logs, tests.jsonl, cases.jsonl and summary.json, and exit 0, 1 or 2.

**Steps:**
1. check-ts;
2. the worker-node and acceptance projects with per-test records;
3. Playwright e2e;
4. scrobbler-e2e;
5. the Python regressions;
6. check-node-bundle (prints the bundle SHA-256);
7. case-map --check-tests without --node-wave, so no target may be pending;
8. goldens;
9. `systemd-analyze --user verify` of the units (blocked, not passed, when systemd-analyze is unavailable);
10. live-noenv;
11. live status.

**scrobbler-e2e** starts the **e2e bundle** worker/dist/node/e2e.mjs (built by `scripts/build-server.ts --e2e` (N3-07) from worker/test/e2e/node-entry.ts (N6-01), which imports run.ts and never main.ts; its feature and protocol inputs are byte-identical to main.mjs per check-bundle) with PUBLIC_ORIGIN https://music.214510.xyz on 127.2.0.1 with a free port. main.mjs itself refuses loopback upstreams and http origins and is never used here (ADR §3.9). It starts fake-upstreams.ts as separate processes: PDS with AS and PLC (packages/atproto/test-support), Jetstream, and Last.fm and ListenBrainz (worker/test/node/support, N1-13). It then drives:
- the real lastfm-ts-api 2.6.2 client (desktop auth, scrobble batch, now playing, getRecentTracks), in a child process started with `node --import scripts/e2e/scrobbler-clients/https-to-loopback.mjs`. lastfm-ts-api always calls node:https request with only hostname, path and timeout, so it cannot reach http://127.2.0.1:<port> by configuration. The preload replaces `https.request` on the node:https module and calls `module.syncBuiltinESMExports()`, reissuing each call with http.request to 127.2.0.1:<port> with the same method, path, headers and body bytes and Host music.214510.xyz; it throws for any other hostname. The client is configured as a user would (hostname music.214510.xyz, path /2.0/);
- byte-faithful replays of Pano (Last.fm mobile session; ListenBrainz with lowercase token and return_msid), multi-scrobbler (web auth flow through /api/auth without a slash), Web Scrobbler (scrobbles and now playing only; its love goes to api.listenbrainz.org and is not replayed) and Navidrome request sequences;
- five replays of one POST /api/v1/scrobbles with one Idempotency-Key through a signed-in cookie jar.

**Asserted for every client:** PDS records, indexing, reads through /2.0 and /1, and exactly-once forwarding. The case-map step asserts that no retirement cites a superseded amendment.

No real network is contacted, and the script never deploys or runs a live gate body.
